Z||000015||My7Fieros||04-05-2001||12:39 AM||||Lets see....Ok, I know how to upload a pic into the forums PIP, but then what? Also, how do I edit, so that it wont come out huge..this is for a sig also remember. Thanx, M7F||||reg||1
Z||000016||Songman||04-05-2001||01:15 AM||||I use Photoshop for all my editing... As you can see above, I made the pic smaller, changed the brightness and contrast and added an embossed look on the edges. Of course, you don't have to do all of that. Lots of programs can change the size. <P>Figure out what program you have on your computer that will work with graphics. Then try these fairly global commands...<P>1) Control-A - This should select the entire image.<P>2) If the selected area has little handles on it, you can just drag it to the size you want. Otherwise, look in the menus for a command that says resize.<P>3) You'll then need to crop out any white areas from making the picture smaller.<P>If all else fails... e-mail me your pics and tell me what you want done to them. I need some pics of your cars for the TN Fiero website anyway...<P>Hope this helps.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cheever2||04-05-2001||01:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR>If the selected area has little handles on it, you can just drag it to the size you want.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>If you do this, use the corners.  That way it will stay in proportion.<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000018||Songman||04-05-2001||02:58 AM||||Yeah, I shoulda mentioned that.... and also, some programs stay proportionate by holding down the shift key as you drag...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
